Oh, the most important thing is to remember that a monster without a
weapon is VERY different than the same monster with a weapon.

Pets are actually in danger of dying if they fight too many
Gnomes/Hobbits that have weapons... especially the ones that are
carrying broad picks.

This means a couple of things...
1) If you see weapons lying around, you might want to move them so that
monsters can't pick them up.  Put them on an Elbereth square, kick them
into a pit, move them to a different level... do something with them.

2) If you know that a monster has a weapon (you might see a message
about a monster wielding a weapon), you might want to retreat with your
pet, and let your pet heal before it fights that monster.

3) If a weapon wielding monster dies, you might want to run up to its
corpse and get its weapon.



